                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "235293775",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198182126445",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 121,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 121,
                            "last_played": 1790112344
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Honestly it gets to a point where you just can't do anything.\nWhat I mean is the game is turn based and each character has a quickness stat. The quickness stat does not increase with levels, nor does it increase with any stat increases. Every character has a base quickness stat and the only way to increase or DECREASE this stat is from equipment. What you will often find is that any character that wears heavy armor will often have a quickness debuff on it. Even without said debuff, you will have encounters where a full 6 enemies attack your party before any of your characters have a chance to do anything. I often found one or two of my characters would be dead before  I could even take one turn with them. There is no counter play, there is nothing to do to stop it, you just get stomped and you can't stop it. I used to love this game as a kid but it has very clear flaws that stop it from being enjoyable.",
